{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I’m Dr. Patel. I’ll be your doctor during this stay. You’re here because of severe nausea and vomiting. Can you tell me what happened this morning?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I woke up feeling nauseous and started vomiting—like 10 times in an hour. It was dark but not bloody. I only ate a muffin for breakfast, nothing unusual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Any belly pain, fever, or changes in bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No belly pain or fever, but my chest and upper stomach hurt a bit from all the retching."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Got it. In the ER, your blood pressure was high and heart rate fast, likely from dehydration. We’ve started IV fluids and anti-nausea meds like Compazine and Reglan."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I usually take domperidone for this. Why aren’t I getting it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Domperidone isn’t available here, and we couldn’t get it brought in. So we’re using Reglan instead, which works similarly to help your stomach empty."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I hope it works. I’ve had this before with my gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your symptoms match your usual flares. We’re also managing your diabetes with insulin through the IV fluids to keep your sugars stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My sugars have been hard to control lately. Is that making this worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can. We found ketones in your urine, which means your body’s burning fat for energy. That can worsen nausea. That’s why we’re giving you dextrose in the IV—to help stop that process."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. Did my blood sugar come down?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was 139 when you arrived, which is okay, but we’re watching closely. We adjusted your insulin sliding scale to keep it steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. My blood pressure’s usually high too. Is that being treated?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, since you couldn’t take pills, we gave IV metoprolol. Now that your vomiting’s slowing, we’ll switch back to your oral meds—metoprolol and lisinopril."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my esophagitis? I’ve been on esomeprazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2198-04-26 15:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still getting your PPI—esomeprazole—daily. It helps with acid reflux, which can sometimes worsen nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still nauseous, but not vomiting as much. Maybe 2–3 times overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s improvement. Your labs show no infection—white count is normal. We also checked your A1c—it’s 7.2%, which is better than last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I’ve been trying to manage it better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also sent a urine test for porphyria because of your repeated episodes. It came back negative, so that’s not the cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the pheochromocytoma test? I remember we talked about that last admission."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We sent plasma metanephrines because your blood pressure was high with symptoms. But the 24-hour urine collection was incomplete—you didn’t follow through."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I forgot to collect it all. Is that a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2198-04-27 08:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means we can’t fully rule out pheo. We’ll discuss it with your GI doctor at follow-up. For now, we’ll focus on getting you stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture showed mixed bacteria, but it’s likely contamination—no infection needing antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I don’t need antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, not for this. Your symptoms are from gastroparesis, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about my breathing? I felt some crackling in my chest yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a chest X-ray yesterday. It’s unchanged—no pneumonia or fluid. Your Port-A-Cath and gastric pacer leads are in place. The crackles likely resolved with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to know. Can I try eating something small?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2198-04-28 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with ice chips and see how you do. If no vomiting, we’ll advance to clear liquids tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2198-04-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You made it through the night with clear liquids. How’s your stomach feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2198-04-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Much better. I had broth and juice, no vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2198-04-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll try a soft diet today—maybe a saltine or toast. If that goes well, you might be ready to go home tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2198-04-29 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s great news. I was worried this would take longer."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2198-04-29 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve responded well. We’ll keep monitoring, but things are looking positive."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You tolerated a full meal last night—no nausea or vomiting. That’s a big step."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes! I had mashed potatoes and chicken. Felt normal for the first time in days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’ll discharge you today. You’ll go home on all your usual meds—domperidone, insulin, blood pressure pills, and PPI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No changes at all?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No changes. Continue domperidone three times a day, insulin as per your sliding scale, and the rest as before. Use Compazine or Zofran if nausea returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my follow-up with GI?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep your scheduled appointment. They’ll review the pheo testing and your overall gastroparesis management."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I worry about the incomplete urine test?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. The GI team will decide if it needs to be repeated. Focus on staying hydrated and eating small, frequent meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thank you for helping me through this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll get the discharge papers ready. A nurse will review everything with you before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, sounds good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing—keep using the scopolamine patch as prescribed. It can help with nausea between flares."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I forgot to put one on before this episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That might have contributed. Try to stay consistent, especially if you feel a flare coming on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make sure to do that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’ll see you at follow-up. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurse will be in shortly with your discharge instructions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll wait for them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Feel free to call your doctor if symptoms return or worsen after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I don’t want to end up back here soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best to help you avoid that. Keep up with your diabetes care and GI follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care and get some rest at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll get your prescriptions sent to your pharmacy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2198-04-30 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re all set. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2198-04-26 15:23:00",
    "admission_end": "2198-04-30 16:30:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 30-year-old woman with Type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis was admitted for intractable nausea and vomiting, unable to tolerate oral intake. She was managed with IV fluids, antiemetics including Reglan as a substitute for non-formulary domperidone, and insulin therapy with D5W to address urinary ketones. Her hypertension was controlled with IV metoprolol initially, then transitioned to oral medications. She gradually advanced her diet, tolerating a full meal by discharge. A chest X-ray showed no new abnormalities, and urine culture indicated contamination without infection. Porphyria testing was negative, though pheochromocytoma evaluation was incomplete due to non-compliance with urine collection. She was discharged home on her prior medications with follow-up scheduled with her GI physician.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Esophagitis, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
